#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.desktop.in:3
#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:7
msgid "Baseboard"
msgstr "Baseboard"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.desktop.in:4
#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:8
#: crates/app/src/application.rs:145
msgid "MSI motherboard sensors and fans"
msgstr "Czujniki i wentylatory płyt MSI"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.desktop.in:10
msgid "sensors;temperature;fan;voltage;hardware;motherboard;mainboard;RGB;"
msgstr ""
"czujniki;temperatura;wentylator;napięcie;sprzęt;płyta "
"główna;płyta;RGB;sensors;"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:7
msgid "Window width"
msgstr "Szerokość okna"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:11
msgid "Window height"
msgstr "Wysokość okna"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:15
msgid "Window maximized"
msgstr "Okno zmaksymalizowane"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:20
#: crates/app/src/preferences.rs:157
msgid "Refresh interval"
msgstr "Odświeżanie"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:21
msgid "Seconds between two readings of the sensors."
msgstr "Sekundy między dwoma odczytami czujników."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:25
#: crates/app/src/preferences.rs:208
msgid "Names from lm-sensors"
msgstr "Nazwy z lm-sensors"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:26
msgid ""
"Name the readings as the sensors command does, where the lm-sensors "
"configuration gives a label."
msgstr ""
"Nazwy odczytów takie jak w poleceniu sensors, gdy konfiguracja lm-sensors "
"podaje etykietę."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:30
msgid "Hidden readings"
msgstr "Ukryte odczyty"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:31
msgid ""
"Readings Baseboard does not show on any page, as chip/channel@device, e.g. "
"nct6687/fan2@devices/platform/nct6683.2592."
msgstr ""
"Odczyty, których Baseboard nie pokazuje na żadnej stronie, jako układ/"
"kanał@urządzenie, np. nct6687/fan2@devices/platform/nct6683.2592."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:35
msgid "Readings turned on"
msgstr "Włączone odczyty"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.gschema.xml:36
msgid ""
"Readings that are off until turned on, such as the numbered temperature "
"sensors of NVMe disks, and that Baseboard shows; as in the hidden readings."
msgstr ""
"Odczyty domyślnie wyłączone, np. numerowane czujniki temperatury dysków "
"NVMe, które Baseboard pokazuje; zapis jak w ukrytych odczytach."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:10
msgid ""
"A native GNOME app for the sensors and fans of MSI motherboards on Linux. "
"Sensor readings work on any board. Fan header names and, later, fan control "
"need a board profile; one is verified today: MAG B850M MORTAR WIFI."
msgstr ""
"Natywna aplikacja GNOME do czujników i wentylatorów płyt głównych MSI w "
"Linuksie. Odczyty czujników działają na każdej płycie. Nazwy złączy, a w "
"przyszłości sterowanie wentylatorami, wymagają profilu płyty; dziś jest "
"jeden sprawdzony: MAG B850M MORTAR WIFI."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:11
msgid ""
"Baseboard shows the temperatures, fan speeds and voltages reported by your "
"motherboard, processor, graphics card, disks and memory, with the names of "
"the fan headers printed on the board."
msgstr ""
"Baseboard pokazuje temperatury, obroty wentylatorów i napięcia zgłaszane "
"przez płytę główną, procesor, kartę graficzną, dyski i pamięć, z nazwami "
"złączy wentylatorów nadrukowanymi na płycie."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:12
msgid ""
"It also shows information about the board, BIOS, processor, memory, graphics "
"card and disks, and copies it as text for bug reports."
msgstr ""
"Pokazuje też informacje o płycie, BIOS-ie, procesorze, pamięci, karcie "
"graficznej i dyskach i kopiuje je jako tekst do zgłoszeń błędów."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:13
msgid ""
"Later versions will also control fans, onboard RGB lighting and power "
"profiles."
msgstr ""
"Kolejne wersje będą też sterować wentylatorami, podświetleniem RGB płyty i "
"profilami energii."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:14
msgid ""
"MSI and MSI product names are trademarks of Micro-Star International Co., "
"Ltd. Baseboard is an independent project and is not affiliated with or "
"endorsed by MSI."
msgstr ""
"MSI i nazwy produktów MSI są znakami towarowymi Micro-Star International "
"Co., Ltd. Baseboard jest niezależnym projektem, niezwiązanym z MSI i bez jej "
"poparcia."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:40
msgid "Readings named after the board’s fan headers and voltage rails"
msgstr "Odczyty nazwane według złączy wentylatorów i szyn napięć płyty"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:45
msgid "The board, BIOS, processor, memory and disks"
msgstr "Płyta, BIOS, procesor, pamięć i dyski"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:50
msgid "The readings in the dark style"
msgstr "Odczyty w ciemnym stylu"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:63
msgid ""
"The first release. Baseboard reads the sensors of a motherboard and shows "
"information about the system; it does not control anything yet."
msgstr ""
"Pierwsze wydanie. Baseboard odczytuje czujniki płyty głównej i pokazuje "
"informacje o systemie; jeszcze niczym nie steruje."

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:65
msgid ""
"Temperatures, fan speeds and voltages; on a board with a profile, named "
"after its fan headers and voltage rails"
msgstr ""
"Temperatury, obroty wentylatorów i napięcia; na płycie z profilem nazwane "
"według jej złączy wentylatorów i szyn napięć"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:66
msgid ""
"Voltages rated against their tolerance, with the lowest and highest value "
"since the app started"
msgstr ""
"Ocena napięć względem tolerancji, z najniższą i najwyższą wartością od "
"uruchomienia aplikacji"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:67
msgid ""
"A System page with the board, BIOS, processor, memory, graphics card, drives "
"and the fan driver, which can be copied as text for bug reports"
msgstr ""
"Strona System z płytą, BIOS-em, procesorem, pamięcią, kartą graficzną, "
"dyskami i sterownikiem wentylatorów, którą można skopiować jako tekst do "
"zgłoszeń błędów"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:68
msgid "English and Polish"
msgstr "Interfejs po angielsku i po polsku"

#: data/me.bojanowski.Baseboard.metainfo.xml.in:70
msgid "Fan control, onboard RGB lighting and power profiles are not there yet."
msgstr ""
"Sterowania wentylatorami, podświetlenia RGB płyty i profili energii jeszcze "
"nie ma."

#. Translators: a CPU fan was spinning and shows 0 rpm now, on the
#. Overview, the Fans page and the System page.
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:20
msgid "CPU fan stopped"
msgstr "Wentylator procesora stoi"

#. Translators: under "CPU fan stopped" on the Fans page.
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:26
msgid "It was spinning earlier and has shown 0 rpm for at least 10 seconds."
msgstr "Kręcił się wcześniej, a od co najmniej 10 s ma 0 rpm."

#. Translators: {rail} is a supply rail, e.g. "+12 V", and {value}
#. what the board reads, e.g. "11.20 V".
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:37
#, rust-format
msgid "{rail} below normal: {value}"
msgstr "Napięcie {rail} poniżej normy: {value}"

#. Translators: {rail} is a supply rail, e.g. "+12 V", and {value}
#. what the board reads, e.g. "12.80 V".
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:41
#, rust-format
msgid "{rail} above normal: {value}"
msgstr "Napięcie {rail} powyżej normy: {value}"

#. Translators: under the warning about a supply rail; {range} is
#. the normal range, e.g. "11.40–12.60 V".
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:49
#, rust-format
msgid ""
"The normal range is {range}. Board readings can be inaccurate; if the "
"computer is unstable, consider checking the power supply."
msgstr ""
"Norma to {range}. Odczyt z płyty bywa niedokładny; jeśli komputer jest "
"niestabilny, warto sprawdzić zasilacz."

#. Translators: the status sentence on top of the Overview; {value}
#. is e.g. "93 °C".
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:65
#, rust-format
msgid "Processor is very hot: {value}"
msgstr "Procesor jest bardzo gorący: {value}"

#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:70
#, rust-format
msgid ""
"At {limit} it starts to slow down so as not to overheat. The fans run at "
"full speed."
msgstr ""
"Przy {limit} zaczyna zwalniać, żeby się nie przegrzać. Wentylatory pracują "
"na pełnych obrotach."

#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:73
#, rust-format
msgid "At {limit} it starts to slow down so as not to overheat."
msgstr "Przy {limit} zaczyna zwalniać, żeby się nie przegrzać."

#. Translators: the status sentence on top of the Overview; {name}
#. is a reading, e.g. "Composite", and {value} e.g. "87 °C".
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:79
#, rust-format
msgid "Very hot: {name}, {value}"
msgstr "Bardzo gorąco: {name}, {value}"

#. Translators: under "Very hot"; {limit} is e.g. "94 °C".
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:83
#, rust-format
msgid "The limit is {limit}."
msgstr "Granica to {limit}."

#. Translators: the status sentence on top of the Overview and the
#. System page.
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:94
msgid "Everything is fine"
msgstr "Wszystko w normie"

#. Translators: the status sentence on top of the Overview and the
#. System page on a board without a profile.
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:101
msgid "Readings work"
msgstr "Odczyty działają"

#. Translators: under the most important problem on the Overview and the
#. System page.
#: crates/app/src/alert.rs:108
#, rust-format
msgid "And {} more problem"
msgid_plural "And {} more problems"
msgstr[0] "I jeszcze {} problem"
msgstr[1] "I jeszcze {} problemy"
msgstr[2] "I jeszcze {} problemów"

#: crates/app/src/application.rs:124
msgid "The nct6683 driver of Linux and its documentation"
msgstr "Sterownik nct6683 w Linuksie i jego dokumentacja"

#: crates/app/src/application.rs:128
msgid "The hwmon sysfs interface of Linux"
msgstr "Interfejs sysfs hwmon w Linuksie"

#: crates/app/src/application.rs:133
msgid "OpenRGB issue reports on the RGB protocol"
msgstr "Zgłoszenia w OpenRGB opisujące protokół RGB"

#. Translators: your name and email, one translator per line.
#: crates/app/src/application.rs:149
msgid "translator-credits"
msgstr "Tomasz Bojanowski"

#: crates/app/src/application.rs:156
msgid "Hardware descriptions from public sources"
msgstr "Opis sprzętu ze źródeł publicznych"

#. Translators: the title of the vertical axis of a fan curve.
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:380
msgid "Duty cycle"
msgstr "Wypełnienie"

#. Translators: the title of the horizontal axis of a fan curve;
#. {source} is a temperature, e.g. "Processor (board sensor)".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:389
#, rust-format
msgid "Temperature: {source}"
msgstr "Temperatura: {source}"

#. Translators: the zone of a fan curve below the lowest duty
#. cycle allowed; {duty} is e.g. "30 %".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:472
#, rust-format
msgid "Below the minimum of {duty}"
msgstr "Poniżej minimum {duty}"

#. Translators: the emergency temperature of the source on a
#. fan curve that must reach full duty by then; e.g.
#. "Emergency threshold 95 °C: 100 % from there".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:514
#, rust-format
msgid "Emergency threshold {temperature}: {duty} from there"
msgstr "Próg awaryjny {temperature}: od niego {duty}"

#. Translators: the emergency temperature of the source on a
#. fan curve, e.g. "Emergency threshold 95 °C".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:520
#, rust-format
msgid "Emergency threshold {temperature}"
msgstr "Próg awaryjny {temperature}"

#. Translators: {source} is a temperature, e.g. "Processor (board sensor)".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:564
#, rust-format
msgid "Temperature source: {source}."
msgstr "Źródło temperatury: {source}."

#. Translators: a point of a fan curve, e.g. "Point 3: 60 °C, 35 %."
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:570 crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:189
#, rust-format
msgid "Point {number}: {temperature}, {duty}."
msgstr "Punkt {number}: {temperature}, {duty}."

#. Translators: read by screen readers for a row of equal points
#. of a fan curve, e.g. "Points 4 to 7: 85 °C, 100 %.".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:574 crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:182
#, rust-format
msgid "Points {first} to {last}: {temperature}, {duty}."
msgstr "Punkty od {first} do {last}: {temperature}, {duty}."

#. Translators: the source temperature and the fan's duty cycle
#. now, e.g. "Now 46.0 °C, duty cycle 38 %."
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:588
#, rust-format
msgid "Now {temperature}, duty cycle {duty}."
msgstr "Teraz {temperature}, wypełnienie {duty}."

#. Translators: the controller changes the duty cycle
#. gradually; {duty} is where it is heading, e.g. "40 %".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:599
#, rust-format
msgid "The fan is moving to {duty}."
msgstr "Wentylator dochodzi do {duty}."

#. Translators: the lowest duty cycle allowed for this fan, e.g. "30 %".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:607
#, rust-format
msgid "Minimum duty cycle: {duty}."
msgstr "Minimalne wypełnienie: {duty}."

#. Translators: the emergency temperature of the source, e.g. "95 °C".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:614
#, rust-format
msgid "Emergency threshold: {temperature}."
msgstr "Próg awaryjny: {temperature}."

#. Translators: the name of the chart for the screen reader;
#. {name} is a fan, e.g. "CPU fan 1".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:758
#, rust-format
msgid "Curve of {name}"
msgstr "Krzywa: {name}"

#. Translators: the label of the operating point on a fan curve,
#. e.g. "Now 46.0 °C · 38 %".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:998
#, rust-format
msgid "Now {temperature} · {duty}"
msgstr "Teraz {temperature} · {duty}"

#. Translators: under the label of the operating point, where
#. the fan is heading, e.g. "target 40 %".
#: crates/app/src/fan_chart.rs:1010
#, rust-format
msgid "target {duty}"
msgstr "cel {duty}"

#. Translators: the source of a fan curve when it is a temperature
#. the kernel driver does not report.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:69
msgid "A temperature the driver does not report"
msgstr "Temperatura, której sterownik nie podaje"

#. Translators: the source of a fan curve when the controller
#. follows no temperature.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:72
msgid "No temperature"
msgstr "Brak temperatury"

#. Translators: the source of a fan curve that follows several
#. temperatures at once; {list} is e.g. "temp1, temp2".
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:80
#, rust-format
msgid "Several temperatures: {list}"
msgstr "Kilka temperatur: {list}"

#. Translators: the part of the project's website on fan control in the
#. kernel, after its address: "/#kernel" on the English page,
#. "/pl/#jadro" on the Polish one. Keep "/#kernel" for a language
#. without its own page.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:95
msgid "/#kernel"
msgstr "/pl/#jadro"

#. Translators: a link after the sentence about the kernel on the
#. Fans page; it opens the website's section on fan control in the
#. kernel.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:114
msgid "Kernel status"
msgstr "Stan w jądrze"

#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:171
msgid "For now, Baseboard only shows the fan settings from the BIOS."
msgstr "Baseboard na razie tylko pokazuje ustawienia wentylatorów z BIOS-u."

#. Translators: in the legend of the fan charts, the hatched zone
#. below the lowest duty cycle of a header.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:200
msgid "below the header's minimum"
msgstr "poniżej minimum złącza"

#. Translators: in the legend of the fan charts, the red dashed line.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:202
msgid "emergency threshold"
msgstr "próg awaryjny"

#. Translators: in the legend of the fan charts, the green dot.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:204
msgid "now: temperature and duty cycle"
msgstr "teraz: temperatura i wypełnienie"

#. Translators: in the legend of the fan charts, the dashed line of
#. a curve before its first point and after its last one.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:207
msgid "curve extension"
msgstr "przedłużenie krzywej"

#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:423 crates/app/src/fans.rs:606
msgid "Fans are speeding up"
msgstr "Wentylatory przyspieszają"

#. Translators: read by screen readers for the list of fans.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:462 crates/app/src/overview.rs:44
#: crates/app/src/overview/summary.rs:545 crates/app/src/window.rs:62
#: crates/app/src/window.ui:63
msgid "Fans"
msgstr "Wentylatory"

#. Translators: Baseboard cannot control the board's fans here.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:639 crates/app/src/system.rs:990
msgid "Fan control unavailable"
msgstr "Sterowanie wentylatorami niedostępne"

#. Translators: {} is the name of the board's chip, e.g. nct6687.
#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:650 crates/app/src/system.rs:997
#, rust-format
msgid "The board's {} chip was not found"
msgstr "Nie znaleziono układu płyty {}"

#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:666 crates/app/src/overview.rs:746
msgid "All readings are hidden"
msgstr "Wszystkie odczyty są ukryte"

#: crates/app/src/fans.rs:667 crates/app/src/overview.rs:747
msgid "Turn them on again in Preferences."
msgstr "Można je włączyć z powrotem w preferencjach."

#: crates/app/src/fans.ui:24 crates/app/src/overview.ui:35
msgid "Reading the sensors…"
msgstr "Odczyt czujników…"

#: crates/app/src/fans.ui:28 crates/app/src/overview.ui:21
#: crates/app/src/window.rs:511
msgid "Details"
msgstr "Szczegóły"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:165
msgid "Automatic BIOS"
msgstr "Automat BIOS"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:166
msgid "Manual"
msgstr "Ręczny"

#. Translators: the mode of a fan when the kernel driver gives none.
#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:168
msgid "The mode could not be read"
msgstr "Nie udało się odczytać trybu"

#. Translators: read by screen readers for the legend under the large
#. chart of a fan curve.
#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:234
msgid "Legend of the chart"
msgstr "Legenda wykresu"

#. Translators: on a fan's row and on its curve page when the
#. board's controller did not give the curve.
#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:259 crates/app/src/fans/row.rs:93
#: crates/app/src/fans/row.rs:165
msgid "The curve could not be read"
msgstr "Nie udało się odczytać krzywej"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:260
msgid "Baseboard tries again every 10 seconds."
msgstr "Baseboard próbuje ponownie co 10 sekund."

#. Translators: on the curve page, the group about the fan
#. header of the board: its mode, minimum and notes.
#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:274
msgid "Header"
msgstr "Złącze"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:277
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "Tryb"

#. Translators: on the curve page of a fan in manual mode.
#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:281
msgid "In manual mode the curve does not run"
msgstr "W trybie ręcznym krzywa nie działa"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:283
msgid ""
"The fan holds a fixed duty cycle, and the curve stays in the board's "
"controller."
msgstr "Wentylator ma stałe wypełnienie, a krzywa zostaje w kontrolerze płyty."

#. Translators: on the curve page, the lowest duty cycle of a
#. header.
#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:289
msgid "Minimum"
msgstr "Minimum"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:290
msgid "The lowest duty cycle Baseboard allows"
msgstr "Najniższe wypełnienie, jakie Baseboard dopuści"

#. Translators: on the curve page of a fan header whose channel
#. nobody has checked on this board.
#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:296 crates/app/src/fans/row.rs:158
msgid "This header was not checked on this board"
msgstr "Złącza nie sprawdzono na tej płycie"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:297
msgid "Nobody has confirmed yet that this reading belongs to this header."
msgstr "Nikt jeszcze nie potwierdził, że ten odczyt należy do tego złącza."

#. Translators: on the curve page of a fan that has not spun
#. since Baseboard started.
#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:303 crates/app/src/fans/row.rs:161
msgid "Not spinning since the app started"
msgstr "Nie kręci się od uruchomienia aplikacji"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:304 crates/app/src/fans/row.rs:162
msgid "The header may be empty."
msgstr "Złącze może być puste."

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:323
msgid "Temperature source"
msgstr "Źródło temperatury"

#. Translators: under "Temperature source" on the curve page; "it"
#. is the temperature.
#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:326
msgid "The controller computes the duty cycle from it."
msgstr "Według niej kontroler liczy wypełnienie."

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:339
msgid "Cannot be changed"
msgstr "Nie można zmienić"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:347
msgid "How the curve works"
msgstr "Jak działa krzywa"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:350
msgid "The duty cycle changes linearly between the points"
msgstr "Między punktami wypełnienie zmienia się liniowo"

#: crates/app/src/fans/curve_page.rs:351
